{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 43, :comments ["<b>O nations, acclaim.</b> You are the arrows and sword of HaShem, so that all may recognize that HaShem is upright and there is no injustice in Him, as it says: יִשְׂמְחוּ וִירַנְּנוּ לְאֻמִּים כִּי תִשְׁפֹּט עַמִּים מִישׁוֹר (Psalms 67:5)." "<b>His people.</b> And acclaim His people — so that they give thanks and a voice of song." "<b>For the blood of His servants He will avenge, and vengeance He will return to His adversaries.</b> And the acclaiming of His people will be on account of the avenging of the blood of His servants and the vengeance He will return to His adversaries for what they did to Israel by way of revenge." "<b>And He will atone His land.</b> Through the desolation that results from them, for what was done upon it." "<b>His people.</b> And He will also atone His people for all they did — the profanation of HaShem and otherwise — through what they suffered in exile, so that He may restore His Presence among them, as it says: יַחְדָּו יְרַנֵּנוּ כִּי עַיִן בְּעַיִן יִרְאוּ בְּשׁוּב ה׳ צִיּוֹן (Isaiah 52:8)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:23:28.448147084Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}